gio draws the kinds itself

the window draws sys/view's runs, one face on one grid
(`gio/ft.go:/grid of one rune a column/`), so the lens's outline and
render are the terminal's in a window: nroff where troff could be. it
would draw the kinds it knows itself (`design/view:/Kinds, never looks/`):
a face for prose and one for code, sizes, a hairline for depth, a count
in a pill, a picture's cells as paths, an image by its path; and the
terminal's cells for any kind it does not. it needs a second face and
its advances, and a layout of its own beside sys/view's, where a click
still names the part it falls on.
